      "brief": {
        "en": "Requirement: ⊥ never holds: no premises are enough to prove it. Following the declaration of ⊥, fill in whether each case’s goal is derivable."
      },
      "hint": [
        { "en": "⊥ has no introduction rule. Under which premises can it be introduced?" },
        {
          "en": "The elimination rule asks for each introduction rule to be considered in turn. With none, what is left to consider?"
        }
